                "3025 = 55²"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "definition",
            "title": "Finite geometric series",
            "content": "**∑_{i=0}^{n} a · rⁱ = a · (rⁿ⁺¹ - 1) / (r - 1)** for r ≠ 1. When r = 1 every term is `a`, so the sum is `(n + 1) · a` (handle separately to avoid division by zero)."
          },
          {
            "type": "definition",
            "title": "Infinite geometric series",
            "content": "If |r| < 1, then `∑_{i=0}^{∞} a · rⁱ = a / (1 - r)`. Diverges otherwise."
          },
          {
            "type": "real_life_example",
            "title": "Where geometric series appear",
            "items": [
              "**Compound interest:** future value = ∑ payments × (1 + r)ⁿ⁻ⁱ.",
              "**Mortgage / installments:** present value of fixed payments uses a geometric series.",
              "**Algorithm analysis:** the cost of a divide-and-conquer algorithm is often a geometric series.",
              "**Saudi STC's tiered data plans:** half-off each successive month for 4 months → geometric sum."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "step_list",
            "title": "Strategy for any sum",
            "items": [
              "1. Pull out constants.",
              "2. Split using linearity if the summand has multiple parts.",
              "3. Adjust bounds with the splitting rule if needed.",
              "4. Apply the right closed-form formula.",
              "5. Simplify the resulting algebra."
            ]
          },
          {
